refused: d398_two_fields_is_refused.cy:21:48, line 21 column 48
21 |         let $n: union.@csup::untagged number = number[i = 1, b = 2];
   |                                                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 what: this builds `number` with 2 fields, and C's union is built by naming exactly the one written
 why:  a C union's fields share the same bytes, so building one names the field it writes (D398)
